    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0ff55cc361264d68b0f58473b8900dc2",
      "statement": "The import script bumps the sidecar revision automatically because it is the reinstall trigger for the archive bytes (the one input the install fingerprint cannot see), flags changed bindings so instantiating users will be asked for them, and round-trip verifies the bytes it wrote since corrupt committed archives would otherwise surface only at install time.",
      "evidence": [
